ARTICLE 13 — TERMINATION

13.1 Termination for material breach. Either of us can terminate these Terms on thirty (30) days written notice if the other materially breaches and does not cure within those thirty (30) days. If you terminate for our material breach, we will refund the unused prepaid portion.

13.2 We can terminate immediately. We can terminate your Account immediately and without prior notice if (a) you violate Section 2.4, (b) you fail to pay any undisputed invoice when due and ignore our reminder for thirty (30) days, (c) you become insolvent or file for bankruptcy, (d) we are required to terminate by law, or (e) FMCSA or another regulator orders us to terminate your Account.

13.3 What happens when this ends. When your Account ends:
(a) the FleetTrace Device will stop reporting to our cloud (you can re-pair it with another carrier's account if your fleet changes hands);
(b) you can export your ELD records, IFTA reports, and Customer Data through the dashboard for thirty (30) days after termination;
(c) we keep ELD records for the period required by 49 C.F.R. § 395.22(i) and IFTA records for four (4) years for audit purposes;
(d) you owe any unpaid fees through the termination date;
(e) Articles 1, 7 (in part), 8, 9, 11, 12, and 14 keep working.

13.4 Hardware on termination. The FleetTrace Device belongs to you. We do not require you to return it. You can keep it as a paperweight, recycle it, or sell it to another FleetTrace customer.

ARTICLE 13 — TERMINATION

13.1 Termination for material breach. Either of us can terminate these Terms on thirty (30) days written notice if the other materially breaches and does not cure within those thirty (30) days. If you terminate for our material breach, we will refund the unused prepaid portion of the subscription fee.

13.2 We can terminate immediately. We can terminate your Account immediately and without prior notice if (a) you violate Section 2.4, (b) you fail to pay any undisputed invoice when due and ignore our reminder for thirty (30) days, (c) you become insolvent or file for bankruptcy, (d) we are required to terminate by law or court order, or (e) you have not used the Service for twelve (12) consecutive months on the Free Tier (we will email you first).

13.3 What happens when this ends. When your Account is terminated:
(a) your access to the Service stops;
(b) you owe any unpaid fees through the termination date;
(c) we delete Customer Code per Section 7.10;
(d) Articles 1, 7 (in part), 8, 9, 11, 12, and 14 keep working.

13.4 No obligation to keep your data after the export window. We are not responsible for data you fail to export within the thirty (30) day window in Section 7.10.

ARTICLE 13 — TERMINATION

13.1 Termination for material breach. Either of us can terminate these terms on thirty (30) days written notice if the other materially breaches and does not cure within those thirty (30) days. If you terminate for our material breach, we will refund the unused prepaid portion.

13.2 We can terminate immediately. We can terminate your Account immediately and without prior notice if (a) you violate Section 2.4, (b) you fail to pay any undisputed invoice when due and ignore our reminder for thirty (30) days, (c) you become insolvent or file for bankruptcy, (d) we are required to terminate by law, or (e) you have not used the Service for ninety (90) consecutive days on the Free Trial.

13.3 What happens when this ends. When your Account ends:
(a) the agent will stop reporting to us;
(b) we will tell the agent to uninstall itself on next check-in (you can also uninstall it manually);
(c) Customer Data is retained for thirty (30) days for export, then deleted per Section 7.10;
(d) you owe any unpaid fees through the termination date;
(e) Articles 1, 7 (in part), 8, 9, 11, 12, and 14 keep working.
